nio: mark the last steps before launchd's execve

Run 619 no longer panics (the phash fix cleared the NULL deref) but the
panel stops at "load_init_program: attempting to load" with no further
progress.  There is no panic pc to resolve, so put panel marks directly
in load_init_program_at_path -- in kern_exec.c, a file whose edits reach
the kernel -- around the final steps before execve.  The next photograph
will name exactly which call does not return.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -7900,6 +7900,9 @@ load_init_program_at_path(proc_t p, user_addr_t scratch_addr, const char* path,
 	/*
 	 * So that init task is set with uid,gid 0 token
 	 */
+	nio_emark("\nnio: LD pre-security-token");
 	set_security_token(p);
+	nio_emark("\nnio: LD post-security-token");
 
+	nio_emark("\nnio: LD pre-execve");
 	return execve(p, &init_exec_args, retval);
 }
